            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0301" n="203" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg203"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Nelson, Bert N./14: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-23T17:00:00+08:00">October 23, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>98. The following telegram has been sent to the Legation: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“October 23, 5 p.m. I sent another telegram to General Ho Yingchin at
                            Chengchow yesterday urging upon him the necessity of obtaining immediate
                            release of Reverend Nelso. I suggested also <pb facs="0302" n="204"
                                xml:id="pg204"/> that he send a special representative to Kwangshan
                            to push plans for release. Have made similar representations to General
                            Ho Chen-chun here.</p>
                        <p>Repeated to Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
